      "body": "## Summary\n\nWith `SGLANG_USE_AITER` unset (the default), `RMSNorm` and `GemmaRMSNorm` on ROCm run `forward_hip` on `vllm._custom_ops`. Both call `fused_add_rms_norm` with six arguments, `(out, input, residual_out, residual, weight, eps)`. vLLM and ROCm/vllm both define it as `fused_add_rms_norm(input, residual, weight, epsilon)` and update `input` and `residual` in place. So every layer with a residual fails:\n\n```\nTypeError: fused_add_rms_norm() takes 4 positional arguments but 6 were given\n```\n\nThe six-argument call came in with #13814 (`RMSNorm`) and #21188 (`GemmaRMSNorm`). The argument order doesn't match aiter's `rmsnorm2d_fwd_with_add` either (its `residual_in` comes before `residual_out`), and `forward_hip` only runs when aiter is off.\n\nThis PR calls the vLLM op on copies of `x` and `residual`, so `forward_hip` stays out-of-place, and fixes the comment that documented the wrong signature.\n\n## End-to-end (MI325X, TP1, `SGLANG_USE_AITER=0`, `Qwen/Qwen3-8B`)\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| startup | `TypeError` above during CUDA-graph capture | serves |\n| GSM8K (`lm_eval`, 200 questions) | n/a | **0.95 / 0.95** (strict / flexible) |\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] End-to-end run above.\n\nFound by [Hyperloom](https://github.com/AMD-AGI/Hyperloom); reviewed and measured by hand.\nHyperloom was optimizing `MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3-MXFP8` on MI325X; the crash showed up in `GemmaRMSNorm` while bisecting MiniMax-M3 with aiter off.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36250248926](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36250248926)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36250248786](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36250248786)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36250248967](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36250248967)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
